<title>UK: Novorossiisk, Tuapse oil ports shut by bad weather.</title>
<headline>Novorossiisk, Tuapse oil ports shut by bad weather.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>High winds and heavy swell forced the closure of the Black Sea oil ports of Novorossiisk and Tuapse on Wednesday, a shipping source said.</p>
<p>&quot;They're closed due to bad weather,&quot; the source said.</p>
<p>Novorossiisk, the main outlet for Russian Urals crude was closed at 6:00 a.m. local time, while Tuapse was closed at midnight.</p>
<p>The source said that several crude tankers were waiting at anchor to load at berths one, two and seven at Novorossiisk, while a gas oil tanker had been loading at berth three when operations were suspended.</p>
<p>Berth two, which was damaged by a storm over the weekend was operational again after 24 hours, the source said.</p>
<p>The other Black Sea oil port of Odessa and the Baltic port of Ventspils were open on Wednesday.</p>
<p>--London Newsroom +44 171 542 5387</p>
